# The generated schema dump stays out of the image on purpose. Rails
# loads it in place of running migrations whenever the target database
# has no migration history, and its auto-generated
# `enable_extension "pg_catalog.plpgsql"` line fails on Azure Database for
# PostgreSQL: plpgsql is already installed there but is not allow-listed
# for non-superusers, so the statement errors out despite being a no-op.
# Editing the line out does not survive the next local db:migrate, which
# regenerates it. Without the file the deployed app migrates from the
# migrations, which are the source of truth anyway.
db/schema.rb
